    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "overview",
      "value": "The major factors affecting how a business is organized include the size and scope of the business, sector and country, tax advantages, disclosure and compliance requirements, and control and coordination requirements.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "flexibility_of_business_structure",
      "value": "Smaller businesses are more flexible, while larger businesses tend to be organized as corporations or partnerships.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "legal_requirements_for_raising_funds",
      "value": "A business that wishes to raise money on a stock market or be owned by a wide range of people will often need to adopt a specific legal form.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "business_operations",
      "value": "Most businesses operate through a separate entity such as a corporation or a partnership, which may be organized by filing charter documents and complying with ongoing obligations.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "limited_liability",
      "value": "Shareholders in a corporation, limited partners in a limited partnership, and members in a limited liability company are typically shielded from personal liability for the entity's debts.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "partnership_terms",
      "value": "The terms of a partnership are partly governed by a partnership agreement and partly by the law of the jurisdiction where the partnership is located.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "sole_proprietorship",
      "value": "A single person who owns and runs a business is known as a sole proprietor, regardless of whether the ownership is direct or through a formally organized entity.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "double_taxation",
      "value": "Corporations may face double taxation, where profits are taxed at the corporate level and again at the individual level when dividends are distributed.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "small_corporation_exemptions",
      "value": "Laws may treat small corporations differently from large ones, allowing exemptions from certain legal filing requirements or labor laws.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "curriculum",
      "field": "initial_public_offering",
      "value": "Going public through an initial public offering (IPO) means that part of the business will be owned by the public and requires tighter disclosure and compliance with laws.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0014",
        "chunk_title": "Business organization",
        "chunk_order": 13,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "definition",
      "value": "When businesses need to raise money, they sometimes offer securities for sale.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0015",
        "chunk_title": "Capital",
        "chunk_order": 14,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "methods_of_raising_capital",
      "value": "Capital may be raised through private means, by an initial public offering (IPO) on a stock exchange, or in multiple other ways.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0015",
        "chunk_title": "Capital",
        "chunk_order": 14,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "major_stock_exchanges",
      "value": "Major stock exchanges include Shanghai Stock Exchange, Singapore Exchange, Hong Kong Stock Exchange, New York Stock Exchange, NASDAQ, London Stock Exchange, Tokyo Stock Exchange, and Bombay Stock Exchange.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0015",
        "chunk_title": "Capital",
        "chunk_order": 14,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "types_of_capital_sourcing",
      "value": "Other types of capital sourcing include crowdsourcing on the Internet, venture capital, bank loans, and debentures.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0015",
        "chunk_title": "Capital",
        "chunk_order": 14,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "definition",
      "value": "Businesses often have important intellectual property that needs protection from competitors for the company to stay profitable.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0016",
        "chunk_title": "Intellectual property",
        "chunk_order": 15,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "types",
      "value": "This could require patents, copyrights, trademarks, or preservation of trade secrets.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0016",
        "chunk_title": "Intellectual property",
        "chunk_order": 15,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "trademarking",
      "value": "Most businesses have names, logos, and similar branding techniques that could benefit from trademarking.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0016",
        "chunk_title": "Intellectual property",
        "chunk_order": 15,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "governance",
      "value": "Patents and copyrights in the United States are largely governed by federal law, while trade secrets and trademarking are mostly a matter of state law.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0016",
        "chunk_title": "Intellectual property",
        "chunk_order": 15,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "protection",
      "value": "A business needs protection in every jurisdiction in which they are concerned about competitors.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
